       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose adds no analgesic benefit.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for inflammatory conditions or pain.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours as needed** for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg per day in total, for example 400 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it. If you want a different dose or frequency, give me the details and I'll enter that. I can also add a note, such as \"take with food.\""
