       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The FDA-approved label for prescription ibuprofen sets a maximum of 3,200 mg/day, and 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. I can't verify that the label says otherwise, and I know of no current labeling that allows this dose. Confirming it doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours as needed**\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, you could talk with pharmacy or the attending about other options. Those could include scheduled acetaminophen alongside the NSAID, or a different class of analgesic. Tell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
